              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What size dehumidifier do I need for my basement?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For a moderately damp basement, plan on 30 to 35 pints up to about 1,500 square feet and 50 pints for larger or wetter spaces. Note that the DOE rating standard changed, so a modern 50-pint unit is roughly equivalent to what was previously sold as 70 pints. Size up for visibly damp basements, but avoid heavily oversizing, which causes short cycling.
