              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do dehumidifiers work in cold basements?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Compressor dehumidifiers lose capacity below about 60 degrees because the coil frosts, and many stop working effectively below 50. Look for a unit with automatic defrost and a stated minimum operating temperature. For unheated basements or crawl spaces that drop into the 40s, a desiccant dehumidifier like the EcoSeb works where compressor units cannot.
